        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148278,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Aprendamos cómo usar funciones para recorrer arrays y manipular sus valores cuando queramos, como cuando presionamos una tecla en un juego.</p><p>Ejecuta el código a continuación que verifica si el valor <code>3</code> existe en el array <code>enemyLevels</code> usando una función.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148279,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Las funciones son útiles cuando queremos ejecutar código reutilizable.</p><p>Para acceder a los elementos del array usando la función <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>, pasemos el array <code>enemyLevels</code> al llamar a la función.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"122\" endIndex=\"133\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>enemyLevels</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148280,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Si queremos acceder a elementos almacenados en múltiples arrays usando la misma función, pasamos los arrays como argumentos al llamar a la función.</p><p>Vamos a codificar el segundo array <code>enemyLevels2</code> al llamar a <code>searchEnemyLevel()</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\":\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"210\" endIndex=\"211\" /><option startIndex=\"212\" endIndex=\"224\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels2 = [\" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, enemyLevels2\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels2);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, enemyLevels2);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>,</code> seguido de <code>enemyLevels2</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148281,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Una vez que hemos pasado un array a una función, podemos iterar sobre los elementos del array. Crea un bucle <code>for</code> para iterar a través de todos los elementos.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" len = enemyLevels.length;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; len; i++) {}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"while\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"{\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"}\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"110\" endIndex=\"113\" /><option startIndex=\"114\" endIndex=\"115\" /><option startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"139\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>for</code> seguido de <code>(</code> y finalmente <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148282,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para recuperar cada elemento del array dentro de un bucle <code>for</code>, usamos la sintaxis <code>array[i]</code>, donde <code>i</code> es la iteración actual, y <code>array</code> es el nombre del array.</p><p>Escribamos el código para recuperar elementos individuales de <code>enemyLevels</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"138\" endIndex=\"152\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(enemyLevels[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>enemyLevels[i]</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148283,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Al usar una función, un array y otro parámetro, podemos hacer mucho.</p><p>Por ejemplo, busquemos el elemento <code>3</code> en el array <code>enemyLevels</code> pasando <code>enemyLevels</code> y luego <code>search</code> a la función <code>searchEnemyLevel</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"262\" endIndex=\"273\" /><option startIndex=\"273\" endIndex=\"274\" /><option startIndex=\"275\" endIndex=\"281\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyLevels = [\" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"enemyLevels, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; enemyLevels.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (enemyLevels[i] === search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enemy level found!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchEnemyLevel(enemyLevels, search);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>enemyLevels</code> seguido de <code>,</code> y finalmente <code>search</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148284,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>También podemos usar múltiples arrays con una función para realizar una acción específica, como encontrar elementos comunes de arrays.</p><p>Vamos a encontrar elementos comunes en dos arrays pasándolos a la función <code>compareArrays</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"263\" endIndex=\"271\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" one = [\" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" two = [\" /><text value=\"90\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"55\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"40\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"compareArrays\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"one, two\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; one.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (one[i] === two[i]) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Same value at this index:&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", one[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"false\" class=\"literal\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"compareArrays(one, two);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>one, two</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148285,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Cómo accedemos a los elementos de un array desde dentro de una función?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Pasamos el array a la función</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Llamamos al array directamente sin pasarlo a la función</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Pasamos el array a la función.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148286,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué muestra este código en la consola?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerScores = [\" /><text value=\"2500\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"displayPlayers\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames, playerScores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerScores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"displayPlayers(playerNames, playerScores);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Muestra múltiples arrays</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Solo muestra el primer array</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Muestra múltiples arrays.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148287,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué podemos usar dentro de una función para iterar sobre un array pasado a la función?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Podemos usar un bucle <code>for</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Podemos usar una declaración <code>if</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Podemos usar un bucle <code>for</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148288,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué sucede cuando usamos <code>playerNames[i]</code> dentro de un bucle <code>for</code> como en la función a continuación?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" playerNames = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Rin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Kai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchPlayer\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"playerNames\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; playerNames.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(playerNames[i]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchPlayer(playerNames);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Recuperamos los elementos del array uno por uno</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Recuperamos los elementos del array todos a la vez</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Recuperamos los elementos del array uno por uno.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148289,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Qué muestra este código en la consola?</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" items = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Key&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" search = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Gem&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchItem\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"items, search\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" i = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"; i &lt; items.length; i++) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  \" /><text value=\"if\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (items[i] == search) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(\" /><text value=\"&quot;The item exists!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"   \" /><text value=\"break\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"  }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" }\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchItem(items, search);\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">No muestra nada</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Muestra <code>The item exists!</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">No muestra nada.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148290,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>¿Por qué pasamos múltiples arrays a una función?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Para realizar una acción específica que incluya información de múltiples arrays</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Para realizar una acción específica que incluya información de solo un array</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Para realizar una acción específica que incluya información de múltiples arrays.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148291,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Al llamar a la función <code>displayScores</code>, codifica el valor para mostrar el array <code>scores</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"106\" endIndex=\"114\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3600\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"displayScores\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(scores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"displayScores(scores);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>(scores)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148292,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Muestra los arrays <code>scores</code> y <code>bonuses</code> pasándolos a la función <code>searchBonus</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&amp;\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"167\" endIndex=\"173\" /><option startIndex=\"173\" endIndex=\"174\" /><option startIndex=\"175\" endIndex=\"182\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"3600\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" bonuses = [\" /><text value=\"50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"150\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"searchBonus\" class=\"title\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"scores, bonuses\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(scores);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(bonuses);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"searchBonus(scores, bonuses);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Asegúrese de elegir <code>scores</code> seguido de <code>,</code> y finalmente <code>bonuses</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #16",
            "id": 148293,
